(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["anatomy-exam-3-female-reproductive-quiz-version-7"]={"title":"Female Reproductive System — Anatomy Exam 3 (Set 7)","category":"Anatomy","sem":"summer-1-2026","questions":[{"q":"Which endometrial layer builds up each month in response to ovarian hormones and is shed at menstruation?","choices":["Stratum functionalis","Stratum basalis layer","Myometrium muscle layer","Perimetrium serosal layer"],"answer":0,"exp":"The stratum functionalis builds up each month in response to ovarian hormones and sloughs off at menstruation. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 43"},{"q":"Just before menstrual flow begins, which vessels open wide and burst, causing the functional layer to slough off?","choices":["Vaginal arteries","Uterine veins","Ovarian arteries","Spiral arteries"],"answer":3,"exp":"Just before menstrual flow starts, the spiral arteries open wide and their capillaries burst, causing the functional layer to slough off. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 43"},{"q":"The pre-embryo typically takes approximately how long to travel from the uterine tube to reach the lumen of the uterus?","choices":["5 to 6 days","10 to 12 days","1 to 2 days","3 weeks"],"answer":0,"exp":"The pre-embryo takes about 5 to 6 days to reach the lumen of the uterus after fertilization in the uterine tube. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 45"},{"q":"The flared, funnel-shaped end of the uterine tube nearest the ovary is called the:","choices":["Ampulla","Interstitial segment","Infundibulum","Isthmus"],"answer":2,"exp":"The infundibulum is the flared end of the uterine tube, bearing the fimbriae, located nearest the ovary. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 45"},{"q":"The long, wide portion of the uterine tube, typically the site of fertilization, is called the:","choices":["Isthmus","Infundibulum","Interstitial segment","Ampulla"],"answer":3,"exp":"The ampulla is the long, wide portion of the uterine tube and the typical site of fertilization. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 45"},{"q":"The narrow portion of the uterine tube that attaches to the uterus is called the:","choices":["Isthmus","Infundibulum","Fimbriae","Ampulla"],"answer":0,"exp":"The isthmus is the narrow portion of the uterine tube attaching to the uterus. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 51"},{"q":"The portion of the uterine tube that passes through the wall of the uterus itself is called the:","choices":["Fimbriated end near the ovary","Interstitial (intramural) segment","Infundibulum with fimbriae","Ampulla of the uterine tube"],"answer":1,"exp":"The interstitial, or intramural, segment is the portion of the uterine tube that passes through the uterine wall. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 51"},{"q":"Cilia lining the walls of the uterine tubes move the oocyte toward the uterus over approximately what time frame?","choices":["3 to 4 hours","2 weeks","5 to 6 days","3 to 4 days"],"answer":3,"exp":"Ciliary movement transports the oocyte toward the uterus over approximately 3 to 4 days. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 52"},{"q":"The uterine (fallopian) tubes are embryologically and functionally homologous to which male structure?","choices":["Epididymis","Seminal vesicle","Vas deferens","Prostate"],"answer":2,"exp":"The uterine tubes are described as homologous to the vas deferens. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 50"},{"q":"Which statement about the relationship between the uterine tube and the ovary is correct?","choices":["The uterine tube physically attaches to the ovary","The uterine tube is fused to the ovarian ligament","The uterine tube penetrates the ovarian cortex","The uterine tube does not physically attach to the ovary"],"answer":3,"exp":"The uterine tube does not physically attach to the ovary; the fimbriae instead sweep the ovulated oocyte into the tube. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 49"},{"q":"The adult vagina measures approximately how long?","choices":["20 cm","15 cm","10 cm","5 cm"],"answer":2,"exp":"The vagina measures about 10 centimeters in length in an adult female. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 56"},{"q":"The vaginal wall consists of three tunics: an inner mucosa, an outer adventitia, and which middle layer?","choices":["Muscularis","Submucosa","Serosa","Perimetrium"],"answer":0,"exp":"The vaginal wall's three tunics are an inner mucosa, a middle muscularis, and an outer adventitia. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 56"},{"q":"The vagina is positioned posterior to which structure and anterior to the rectum?","choices":["The bladder","The urethra","The uterus","The cervix"],"answer":1,"exp":"The vagina extends posterior to the urethra and anterior to the rectum. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 57"},{"q":"The embryonic remnant mucous membrane partially covering the vaginal entry is the:","choices":["Fornix","Frenulum","Prepuce","Hymen"],"answer":3,"exp":"The hymen is the embryonic remnant mucous membrane covering the vaginal entry. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 59"},{"q":"The pocket-like recess surrounding the uterine cervix within the vagina, used for surgical access to the pelvic cavity and for locating certain birth control devices, is the:","choices":["Fornix","Vestibule","Hymen","Isthmus"],"answer":0,"exp":"The fornix is the pocket surrounding the uterine cervix within the vagina. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 60"},{"q":"The cervix attaches to the vagina at approximately what angle?","choices":["120 degrees","180 degrees (straight line)","45 degrees","90 degrees"],"answer":3,"exp":"The cervix attaches to the vagina at approximately a 90-degree angle. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 60"},{"q":"Which muscle related to the vagina is part of the levator ani?","choices":["External urethral sphincter","Urethrovaginal sphincter","Bulbospongiosus","Pubovaginalis"],"answer":3,"exp":"The pubovaginalis muscle, related to the vagina, is part of the levator ani. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 62"},{"q":"Lymphatic drainage of the superior vagina is directed to which nodes?","choices":["Superficial inguinal nodes only","Axillary lymph node chain","Internal and external iliac nodes","Sacral lymph nodes only"],"answer":2,"exp":"The superior vagina drains to the internal and external iliac nodes. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 64"},{"q":"Lymphatic drainage of the inferior vagina includes sacral and common iliac nodes as well as which additional nodes?","choices":["Superficial inguinal nodes","Axillary lymph node chain","Lumbar para-aortic nodes","Deep cervical lymph nodes"],"answer":0,"exp":"The inferior vagina drains to sacral and common iliac nodes as well as the superficial inguinal nodes. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 64"},{"q":"The collective term for the external sex organs of the female is the:","choices":["Vulva (pudendum)","Perineal region","Vaginal vestibule","Mons pubis mound"],"answer":0,"exp":"The external sex organs of the female are collectively called the vulva, also called the pudendum. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 66"},{"q":"The labia majora are embryologically derived from the same structures as which male structure?","choices":["The epididymis","The prostate","The scrotum","The penis"],"answer":2,"exp":"The labia majora are derived from the same embryonic structures as the scrotum. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 73"},{"q":"Which statement correctly distinguishes the labia majora from the labia minora?","choices":["Both the labia majora and labia minora develop coarse pubic hair equally after puberty","The labia majora develop pubic hair after puberty, while the labia minora have no hair or fat","Both the labia majora and labia minora remain completely hairless and fat-free","The labia majora have no hair or fat, while the labia minora develop hair after puberty"],"answer":1,"exp":"The labia majora develop pubic hair after puberty and contain sweat/sebaceous glands, while the labia minora have no hair and no fat. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 73"},{"q":"The labia minora contain a core of spongy connective tissue containing erectile tissue and many small:","choices":["Lymph nodes","Sweat glands","Blood vessels","Sebaceous glands"],"answer":2,"exp":"The labia minora's core of spongy connective tissue contains erectile tissue and many small blood vessels. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 74"},{"q":"Anteriorly, the labia minora form the prepuce of the clitoris; posteriorly, they form the:","choices":["Crura of the clitoral body","Frenulum of the clitoris","Bulb of the vestibule tissue","Glans of the clitoris"],"answer":1,"exp":"Posteriorly, the labia minora form the frenulum of the clitoris. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 74"},{"q":"The clitoris contains two crura and two of which erectile structure?","choices":["Corpus spongiosum","Vestibular bulbs","Glans only","Corpora cavernosa"],"answer":3,"exp":"The clitoris contains two crura and two corpora cavernosa. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 76"},{"q":"The greater vestibular gland is homologous to which male structure?","choices":["Paired seminal vesicle glands","Male prostate gland tissue","Epididymal duct coiling","Bulbourethral (Cowper's) gland"],"answer":3,"exp":"The greater vestibular gland is homologous to the bulbourethral (Cowper's) gland in males. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 78"},{"q":"The greater vestibular gland is located under or behind which structure and drains by a duct into the vestibule?","choices":["The clitoral body and glans","The labia majora fold","The bulb of the vestibule","The mons pubis mound"],"answer":2,"exp":"The greater vestibular gland lies under or behind the bulb of the vestibule and drains via a duct into the vestibule. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 78"},{"q":"The breast is described as extending between which ribs?","choices":["2nd and 6th ribs","4th and 8th ribs","1st and 5th ribs","3rd and 7th ribs"],"answer":0,"exp":"The breast lies between the 2nd and 6th ribs, from the sternal edge to the midaxillary line. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 79"},{"q":"Approximately what fraction of the breast is superficial to the pectoral muscle, versus superficial to the serratus anterior?","choices":["1/3 pectoral, 2/3 serratus anterior","2/3 pectoral, 1/3 serratus anterior","All breast tissue overlies the pectoral muscle only","1/2 pectoral, 1/2 serratus anterior"],"answer":1,"exp":"About two-thirds of the breast lies superficial to the pectoral muscle, with the remaining one-third superficial to the serratus anterior. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 79"},{"q":"The lateral quadrants of the breast receive blood supply from pectoral branches of the thoracoacromial artery and which additional named branch?","choices":["Anterior intercostal perforating artery branches","Subscapular and thoracodorsal artery branches","External mammary branch of the lateral thoracic artery","Perforating branches of the internal thoracic artery"],"answer":2,"exp":"The lateral quadrants of the breast receive supply from pectoral branches of the thoracoacromial artery and the external mammary branch of the lateral thoracic artery. — Female Reproductive Tract for lecure.pptx, Slide 85"}]};
